                 ⚠ SCOPE, narrower than upstream, and a re-expression.
                 · Upstream works in doubles and divides before it multiplies
                   (gain1 + (angle-angle1)*((gain2-gain1)/(angle2-angle1))).
                   This core works in whole tenths of a degree and tenths of a
                   decibel, multiplies before it divides, and truncates toward
                   zero. The two agree only in exact arithmetic. The theorems
                   are about the whole-unit re-expression.
                 · The linear-power interpolation branch (linearGainInterpolation
                   true, via pdBtoLinear/pLinearTodB) is NOT modelled.
                 · The search over the sorted table (lines 82-91) is NOT
                   modelled. The wrap theorems take only the first and last
                   azimuths as given, with First <= Last as the sortedness
                   they rely on.
                 · Tables of zero or one entry (lines 70-74) are not modelled.
                 · Gains are bounded to -100.0 .. +100.0 dB; azimuths to
                   0.0 .. 359.9 degrees, as the header comment states.

                 GRADING THE FIVE CONTRACTS HONESTLY, so nobody has to.
                 · Interpolated_Gain's band (the result never leaves the band
                   between the two neighbouring gains) and Ends_At_Second (the
                   interpolation returns exactly the second entry's gain at its
                   own azimuth, which needs (D*X)/D = X of integer division)
                   carry the weight. Two of three solvers alone cannot
                   discharge them; see below.
                 · Starts_At_First is immediate — the offset is zero.
                 · Wrap_Below_Catches and Wrap_Above_Catches follow from the
                   azimuth domain alone. Their value is what they say about the
                   code, not their difficulty: the fall-through `return 0` at
